24 17:58:07'),(1237,'DOC-1014','BD-2000-0058','Atorvastatin works best when taken at bedtime to target peak hepatic cholesterol synthesis. Continue taking it nightly.',1,'2026-08-24 18:43:07'),(1238,'BD-2000-0058','DOC-1014','Should I be concerned about muscle soreness or liver enzymes?',1,'2026-08-24 19:28:07'),(1239,'DOC-1014','BD-2000-0058','Mild fatigue is rare, but report any severe unexplained muscle cramps. We will recheck liver enzymes and lipid levels in 8 weeks.',1,'2026-08-24 20:13:07'),(1240,'BD-2000-0058','DOC-1015','Dr. Tanvir, I get throbbing one-sided headaches preceded by bright zigzag lines in my visual field.',1,'2026-08-21 17:58:07'),(1241,'DOC-1015','BD-2000-0058','These are classic migraine episodes with aura. Take Naproxen 500mg immediately when the visual aura begins, before the pain peaks.',1,'2026-08-21 18:43:07'),(1242,'BD-2000-0058','DOC-1015','Should I avoid specific dietary triggers like aged cheese or caffeine?',1,'2026-08-21 19:28:07'),(1243,'DOC-1015','BD-2000-0058','Yes, maintain a regular sleep schedule, stay hydrated, and note down food triggers in your daily health journal.',0,'2026-08-21 20:13:07'),(1244,'BD-2000-0058','DOC-1016','Doctor, my TSH is 5.8 mIU/L on Levothyroxine 50mcg. I still feel unusually cold and sluggish in the morning.',1,'2026-08-18 17:58:07'),(1245,'DOC-1016','BD-2000-0058','Your dose requires a slight adjustment. Increase Levothyroxine to 75mcg daily, taken with plain water 45 minutes before breakfast.',1,'2026-08-18 18:43:07'),(1246,'BD-2000-0058','DOC-1016','Can I take my calcium and vitamin D tablets together with the thyroid pill?',1,'2026-08-18 19:28:07'),(1247,'DOC-1016','BD-2000-0058','No, calcium binds to thyroxine and blocks absorption. Separate calcium supplements by at least 4 hours.',1,'2026-08-18 20:13:07'),(1248,'BD-2000-0059','DOC-1015','Good morning Doctor, I have been taking Amlodipine 5mg for 4 days as prescribed, but feel slightly lightheaded around noon. Should I adjust the timing?',1,'2026-08-23 17:59:07'),(1249,'DOC-1015','BD-2000-0059','Hello! Mild lightheadedness can happen initially as peripheral vascular resistance drops. Please check your blood pressure at noon and take the tablet right after breakfast with a glass of water.',1,'2026-08-23 18:44:07'),(1250,'BD-2000-0059','DOC-1015','Understood Doctor. Should I strictly restrict dietary salt, and are 30-minute morning brisk walks safe?',1,'2026-08-23 19:29:07'),(1251,'DOC-1015','BD-2000-0059','Keep sodium under 2g daily. Moderate walks are safe and strongly encouraged. If systolic drops below 100 mmHg, message me immediately.',1,'2026-08-23 20:14:07'),(1252,'BD-2000-0059','DOC-1016','Doctor, my fasting blood glucose was 7.8 mmol/L and 2-hour post-meal was 11.2 mmol/L. I am taking Metformin 500mg twice daily.',1,'2026-08-20 17:59:07'),(1253,'DOC-1016','BD-2000-0059','Thank you for tracking. Since post-prandial remains above our 8.5 target, ensure you take Metformin with meals and minimize refined carbohydrates in your evening diet.',1,'2026-08-20 18:44:07'),(1254,'BD-2000-0059','DOC-1016','Should I schedule an HbA1c and kidney function test before our upcoming clinic review?',1,'2026-08-20 19:29:07'),(1255,'DOC-1016','BD-2000-0059','Yes, please complete an HbA1c and serum creatinine test next week, then upload the PDF report directly to your xMED vault.',1,'2026-08-20 20:14:07'),(1256,'BD-2000-0059','DOC-1016','Will do Doctor, uploaded last month’s lipid panel as well.',1,'2026-08-20 20:59:07'),(1257,'BD-2000-0059','DOC-1017','Hello Doctor, I developed a sudden fever of 102°F yesterday with retro-orbital eye pain and severe body ache. Could this be dengue?',1,'2026-08-17 17:59:07'),(1258,'DOC-1017','BD-2000-0059','Given seasonal trends, do NOT take any Ibuprofen or Aspirin. Take only Paracetamol 500mg up to every 6 hours and drink plenty of ORS and coconut water.',1,'2026-08-17 18:44:07'),(1259,'BD-2000-0059','DOC-1017','Should I get a Complete Blood Count (CBC) and Dengue NS1 antigen test don