9:33:07'),(1356,'DOC-1011','BD-2000-0063','You can repeat 2 puffs after 20 minutes once. If chest indrawing or breathlessness appears, visit our emergency center immediately.',0,'2026-08-22 20:18:07'),(1357,'BD-2000-0064','DOC-1010','Hello Doctor, the red itchy rash on my forearms has flared up after using synthetic laundry powder.',1,'2026-08-14 18:04:07'),(1358,'DOC-1010','BD-2000-0064','Apply the Hydrocortisone cream thinly twice daily for 5 days only, followed by liberal amounts of plain petroleum jelly.',1,'2026-08-14 18:49:07'),(1359,'BD-2000-0064','DOC-1010','Can I take an antihistamine like Cetirizine 10mg at night for the itching?',1,'2026-08-14 19:34:07'),(1360,'DOC-1010','BD-2000-0064','Yes, Cetirizine 10mg at bedtime will relieve nighttime itching and help you rest without scratching.',0,'2026-08-14 20:19:07'),(1361,'BD-2000-0064','DOC-1011','Good afternoon Doctor, my abdominal surgical incision looks slightly pink, but there is no fever or pus.',1,'2026-08-24 18:04:07'),(1362,'DOC-1011','BD-2000-0064','Mild pink erythema is normal during surgical wound remodeling. Keep the area completely dry and clean with sterile dressing.',1,'2026-08-24 18:49:07'),(1363,'BD-2000-0064','DOC-1011','When should I visit the outpatient clinic for suture removal?',1,'2026-08-24 19:34:07'),(1364,'DOC-1011','BD-2000-0064','Please visit the surgical OPD this Thursday between 9 AM and 1 PM for stitch removal and scar assessment.',1,'2026-08-24 20:19:07'),(1365,'BD-2000-0064','DOC-1012','Doctor, my fasting lipid profile shows LDL 155 mg/dL. I have started Atorvastatin 10mg nightly.',1,'2026-08-21 18:04:07'),(1366,'DOC-1012','BD-2000-0064','Atorvastatin works best when taken at bedtime to target peak hepatic cholesterol synthesis. Continue taking it nightly.',1,'2026-08-21 18:49:07'),(1367,'BD-2000-0064','DOC-1012','Should I be concerned about muscle soreness or liver enzymes?',1,'2026-08-21 19:34:07'),(1368,'DOC-1012','BD-2000-0064','Mild fatigue is rare, but report any severe unexplained muscle cramps. We will recheck liver enzymes and lipid levels in 8 weeks.',1,'2026-08-21 20:19:07'),(1369,'BD-2000-0064','DOC-1013','Dr. Tanvir, I get throbbing one-sided headaches preceded by bright zigzag lines in my visual field.',1,'2026-08-18 18:04:07'),(1370,'DOC-1013','BD-2000-0064','These are classic migraine episodes with aura. Take Naproxen 500mg immediately when the visual aura begins, before the pain peaks.',1,'2026-08-18 18:49:07'),(1371,'BD-2000-0064','DOC-1013','Should I avoid specific dietary triggers like aged cheese or caffeine?',1,'2026-08-18 19:34:07'),(1372,'DOC-1013','BD-2000-0064','Yes, maintain a regular sleep schedule, stay hydrated, and note down food triggers in your daily health journal.',0,'2026-08-18 20:19:07'),(1373,'BD-2000-0064','DOC-1014','Doctor, my TSH is 5.8 mIU/L on Levothyroxine 50mcg. I still feel unusually cold and sluggish in the morning.',1,'2026-08-15 18:04:07'),(1374,'DOC-1014','BD-2000-0064','Your dose requires a slight adjustment. Increase Levothyroxine to 75mcg daily, taken with plain water 45 minutes before breakfast.',1,'2026-08-15 18:49:07'),(1375,'BD-2000-0064','DOC-1014','Can I take my calcium and vitamin D tablets together with the thyroid pill?',1,'2026-08-15 19:34:07'),(1376,'DOC-1014','BD-2000-0064','No, calcium binds to thyroxine and blocks absorption. Separate calcium supplements by at least 4 hours.',1,'2026-08-15 20:19:07'),(1377,'BD-2000-0065','DOC-1013','Good morning Doctor, I have been taking Amlodipine 5mg for 4 days as prescribed, but feel slightly lightheaded around noon. Should I adjust the timing?',1,'2026-08-20 18:05:07'),(1378,'DOC-1013','BD-2000-0065','Hello! Mild lightheadedness can happen initially as peripheral vascular resistance drops. Please check your blood pressure at noon and take the tablet right after breakfast with a glass of water.',1,'2026-08-20 18:50:07'),(1379,'BD-2000-0065','DOC-1013','Understood Doctor. Should I strictly restrict dietary salt, and are 30-minute morn