iately when the visual aura begins, before the pain peaks.',1,'2026-08-23 19:05:07'),(1715,'BD-2000-0080','DOC-1001','Should I avoid specific dietary triggers like aged cheese or caffeine?',1,'2026-08-23 19:50:07'),(1716,'DOC-1001','BD-2000-0080','Yes, maintain a regular sleep schedule, stay hydrated, and note down food triggers in your daily health journal.',1,'2026-08-23 20:35:07'),(1717,'BD-2000-0080','DOC-1002','Doctor, my TSH is 5.8 mIU/L on Levothyroxine 50mcg. I still feel unusually cold and sluggish in the morning.',1,'2026-08-20 18:20:07'),(1718,'DOC-1002','BD-2000-0080','Your dose requires a slight adjustment. Increase Levothyroxine to 75mcg daily, taken with plain water 45 minutes before breakfast.',1,'2026-08-20 19:05:07'),(1719,'BD-2000-0080','DOC-1002','Can I take my calcium and vitamin D tablets together with the thyroid pill?',1,'2026-08-20 19:50:07'),(1720,'DOC-1002','BD-2000-0080','No, calcium binds to thyroxine and blocks absorption. Separate calcium supplements by at least 4 hours.',1,'2026-08-20 20:35:07'),(1721,'BD-2000-0081','DOC-1001','Good morning Doctor, I have been taking Amlodipine 5mg for 4 days as prescribed, but feel slightly lightheaded around noon. Should I adjust the timing?',1,'2026-08-25 18:21:07'),(1722,'DOC-1001','BD-2000-0081','Hello! Mild lightheadedness can happen initially as peripheral vascular resistance drops. Please check your blood pressure at noon and take the tablet right after breakfast with a glass of water.',1,'2026-08-25 19:06:07'),(1723,'BD-2000-0081','DOC-1001','Understood Doctor. Should I strictly restrict dietary salt, and are 30-minute morning brisk walks safe?',1,'2026-08-25 19:51:07'),(1724,'DOC-1001','BD-2000-0081','Keep sodium under 2g daily. Moderate walks are safe and strongly encouraged. If systolic drops below 100 mmHg, message me immediately.',1,'2026-08-25 20:36:07'),(1725,'BD-2000-0081','DOC-1002','Doctor, my fasting blood glucose was 7.8 mmol/L and 2-hour post-meal was 11.2 mmol/L. I am taking Metformin 500mg twice daily.',1,'2026-08-22 18:21:07'),(1726,'DOC-1002','BD-2000-0081','Thank you for tracking. Since post-prandial remains above our 8.5 target, ensure you take Metformin with meals and minimize refined carbohydrates in your evening diet.',1,'2026-08-22 19:06:07'),(1727,'BD-2000-0081','DOC-1002','Should I schedule an HbA1c and kidney function test before our upcoming clinic review?',1,'2026-08-22 19:51:07'),(1728,'DOC-1002','BD-2000-0081','Yes, please complete an HbA1c and serum creatinine test next week, then upload the PDF report directly to your xMED vault.',1,'2026-08-22 20:36:07'),(1729,'BD-2000-0081','DOC-1002','Will do Doctor, uploaded last month’s lipid panel as well.',0,'2026-08-22 21:21:07'),(1730,'BD-2000-0081','DOC-1003','Hello Doctor, I developed a sudden fever of 102°F yesterday with retro-orbital eye pain and severe body ache. Could this be dengue?',1,'2026-08-19 18:21:07'),(1731,'DOC-1003','BD-2000-0081','Given seasonal trends, do NOT take any Ibuprofen or Aspirin. Take only Paracetamol 500mg up to every 6 hours and drink plenty of ORS and coconut water.',1,'2026-08-19 19:06:07'),(1732,'BD-2000-0081','DOC-1003','Should I get a Complete Blood Count (CBC) and Dengue NS1 antigen test done today?',1,'2026-08-19 19:51:07'),(1733,'DOC-1003','BD-2000-0081','Yes, get a CBC and NS1 antigen test today. If platelets drop below 100,000 or you notice severe abdominal pain, proceed to the hospital emergency triage.',1,'2026-08-19 20:36:07'),(1734,'BD-2000-0081','DOC-1004','Dr. Kabir, I have severe burning in my upper chest at night, despite taking Omeprazole 20mg daily.',1,'2026-08-16 18:21:07'),(1735,'DOC-1004','BD-2000-0081','Make sure you take Omeprazole 30 minutes before breakfast on an empty stomach. Avoid spicy dinners and do not lie flat within 2 hours of eating.',1,'2026-08-16 19:06:07'),(1736,'BD-2000-0081','DOC-1004','Can I take a chewable antacid if nighttime burning wakes me up?',1,'2026-08-16 19:51:07'),(1737,'DOC-1004','BD-2000-0081','Y