ng and help you rest without scratching.',1,'2026-08-16 20:41:07'),(1834,'BD-2000-0086','DOC-1017','Good afternoon Doctor, my abdominal surgical incision looks slightly pink, but there is no fever or pus.',1,'2026-08-26 18:26:07'),(1835,'DOC-1017','BD-2000-0086','Mild pink erythema is normal during surgical wound remodeling. Keep the area completely dry and clean with sterile dressing.',1,'2026-08-26 19:11:07'),(1836,'BD-2000-0086','DOC-1017','When should I visit the outpatient clinic for suture removal?',1,'2026-08-26 19:56:07'),(1837,'DOC-1017','BD-2000-0086','Please visit the surgical OPD this Thursday between 9 AM and 1 PM for stitch removal and scar assessment.',1,'2026-08-26 20:41:07'),(1838,'BD-2000-0086','DOC-1018','Doctor, my fasting lipid profile shows LDL 155 mg/dL. I have started Atorvastatin 10mg nightly.',1,'2026-08-23 18:26:07'),(1839,'DOC-1018','BD-2000-0086','Atorvastatin works best when taken at bedtime to target peak hepatic cholesterol synthesis. Continue taking it nightly.',1,'2026-08-23 19:11:07'),(1840,'BD-2000-0086','DOC-1018','Should I be concerned about muscle soreness or liver enzymes?',1,'2026-08-23 19:56:07'),(1841,'DOC-1018','BD-2000-0086','Mild fatigue is rare, but report any severe unexplained muscle cramps. We will recheck liver enzymes and lipid levels in 8 weeks.',0,'2026-08-23 20:41:07'),(1842,'BD-2000-0086','DOC-1019','Dr. Tanvir, I get throbbing one-sided headaches preceded by bright zigzag lines in my visual field.',1,'2026-08-20 18:26:07'),(1843,'DOC-1019','BD-2000-0086','These are classic migraine episodes with aura. Take Naproxen 500mg immediately when the visual aura begins, before the pain peaks.',1,'2026-08-20 19:11:07'),(1844,'BD-2000-0086','DOC-1019','Should I avoid specific dietary triggers like aged cheese or caffeine?',1,'2026-08-20 19:56:07'),(1845,'DOC-1019','BD-2000-0086','Yes, maintain a regular sleep schedule, stay hydrated, and note down food triggers in your daily health journal.',1,'2026-08-20 20:41:07'),(1846,'BD-2000-0086','DOC-1020','Doctor, my TSH is 5.8 mIU/L on Levothyroxine 50mcg. I still feel unusually cold and sluggish in the morning.',1,'2026-08-17 18:26:07'),(1847,'DOC-1020','BD-2000-0086','Your dose requires a slight adjustment. Increase Levothyroxine to 75mcg daily, taken with plain water 45 minutes before breakfast.',1,'2026-08-17 19:11:07'),(1848,'BD-2000-0086','DOC-1020','Can I take my calcium and vitamin D tablets together with the thyroid pill?',1,'2026-08-17 19:56:07'),(1849,'DOC-1020','BD-2000-0086','No, calcium binds to thyroxine and blocks absorption. Separate calcium supplements by at least 4 hours.',1,'2026-08-17 20:41:07'),(1850,'BD-2000-0087','DOC-1019','Good morning Doctor, I have been taking Amlodipine 5mg for 4 days as prescribed, but feel slightly lightheaded around noon. Should I adjust the timing?',1,'2026-08-22 18:27:07'),(1851,'DOC-1019','BD-2000-0087','Hello! Mild lightheadedness can happen initially as peripheral vascular resistance drops. Please check your blood pressure at noon and take the tablet right after breakfast with a glass of water.',1,'2026-08-22 19:12:07'),(1852,'BD-2000-0087','DOC-1019','Understood Doctor. Should I strictly restrict dietary salt, and are 30-minute morning brisk walks safe?',1,'2026-08-22 19:57:07'),(1853,'DOC-1019','BD-2000-0087','Keep sodium under 2g daily. Moderate walks are safe and strongly encouraged. If systolic drops below 100 mmHg, message me immediately.',1,'2026-08-22 20:42:07'),(1854,'BD-2000-0087','DOC-1020','Doctor, my fasting blood glucose was 7.8 mmol/L and 2-hour post-meal was 11.2 mmol/L. I am taking Metformin 500mg twice daily.',1,'2026-08-19 18:27:07'),(1855,'DOC-1020','BD-2000-0087','Thank you for tracking. Since post-prandial remains above our 8.5 target, ensure you take Metformin with meals and minimize refined carbohydrates in your evening diet.',1,'2026-08-19 19:12:07'),(1856,'BD-2000-0087','DOC-1020','Should I schedule an HbA1c and kidney function test before our upcoming clinic 